      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{63c199d2c7d7907610c71afd|full_name} For sure. Thanks for the feedback.\n\nIn my head, this could be a layer in-between the group tab in notifications, and the notifications themselves.\n\nSay, for example, you have a \"GroupListItem\" component which had all of the notifications for a given group underneath it. You can click it to reveal, like a sublist. \n\nThis would mean I could at least quickly scroll the groups themselves, and only expand ones I really care about. It even just should be faster to scroll since you can prioritize, similar to the effect of a numbered list vs. the same numbered list but randomized (which is what notifications kind of are like currently).",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
